<title>FRANCE: Axa denies plans to sell Suez stake.</title>
<headline>Axa denies plans to sell Suez stake.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>French insurer Axa said on Tuesday has no plans to sell its stake in Cie de Suez after it merges with Unions des Assurance de Paris.</p>
<p>&quot;We have no intention of selling our stake in Suez, which for us is a long term investment,&quot; an Axa spokeswoman told Reuters.  </p>
<p>After its merger with UAP the new company will hold about 7.5 percent of Suez.</p>
<p>The spokeswoman was commenting on rumours in the French stockmarket and a newspaper report that Axa would shed its Suez stake and other shareholdings in large French companies in the months ahead.</p>
<p>&quot;All our shareholdings are long term investments and any sales will not be spectacular,&quot; the spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>Financial daily La Tribune reported on Tuesday rumours that Axa was considering selling stakes in Saint Gobain, Elf, Galeries Lafayette, Lyonaise des Eaux and Generale des Eaux among others.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5071</p>
